WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.350
Kevin Feige, the main architect behind the
Marvel Cinematic Universe, was recently promoted

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.430
to oversee everything Marvel-related for parent
company Disney not just his traditional territory

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:11.760
of Marvel Studios.

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:16.600
And that promotion means that Feige is wresting
full control of the television side of Marvel

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.460
from the company's CEO Ike Perlmutter and
Head of Television Jeph Loeb.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.880
Loeb's departure from the company has just
recently been announced, as new reports indicate

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.120
that Marvel hasn't been pleased over recent
developments on the company's television side.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.880
Specifically, Marvel Television executives
were reportedly "shocked and embarrassed"

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:38.710
that Hulu decided to cancel the planned live-action
Ghost Rider series before a single episode

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.460
had aired, according to a report from Variety.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.850
The streaming platform pulled the plug on
Ghost Rider in September 2019, just a few

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:50.070
months after it was announced in May 2019
that the project was in development.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:54.240
"I don't know who the hell you are, but you
just made a big mistake."

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.220
"Funny, I was going to say the same thing,
without the accent."

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.720
Ghost Rider was meant to be an off-shoot of
the long-running ABC show Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.,

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:07.579
arguably the most successful live-action Marvel
TV series to date, but wouldn't actually have

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.720
any ties to that series' storyline.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.329
The only connection it would have to Agents
of S.H.I.E.L.D. was through Gabriel Luna,

00:01:13.329 --> 00:01:17.509
who was set to star on Ghost Rider as the
namesake flaming-skull-headed hero, which

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:21.500
the actor had previously portrayed during
a number of guest appearances on Agents of

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.000
S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.680
According to Deadline, Hulu and the creative
team behind Ghost Rider hit, quote, "a creative

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.860
impasse which could not be resolved."

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.780
Since coming to an agreement was apparently
impossible and the differences between the

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:37.530
streamer and the show's team were evidently
irreconcilable, Hulu executives decided not

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.220
to move forward with the series.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.380
That happened in late September 2019, and
a month later, it's still unclear what exactly

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.140
the creative roadblock entailed.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.770
The intention was to totally revamp Ghost
Rider for the Marvel-Hulu series, and have

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:54.320
him stand as a new version of the character,
separate from the Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:54.820
narrative.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.820
That's a confusing setup at best, and it doesn't
seem out of the realm of possibility that

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:04.760
Hulu executives grew unhappy with how the
Ghost Rider team planned to portray the antihero.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.319
It seems the failure of Ghost Rider should
have been the writing on the wall that big

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.560
changes were on the way for the Marvel Television
team, and now those changes have arrived.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.900
But what does this all mean for the future
of Marvel Television?

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.810
If you've noticed that Marvel movies have
become more diverse and taken bigger risks

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.680
over the last few years, that's no coincidence.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.300
Prior to 2015, Feige and CEO Ike Perlmutter
shared control over Marvel Studios, meaning

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.160
both executives had say over what ultimately
ended up on the screen.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:37.260
The problem with that set-up was that the
two rarely agreed on anything, and in 2015,

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.140
Disney head Bob Iger made the decision to
effectively split Marvel in half.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:46.220
The movie side of the business, Marvel Studios,
would be handled by Feige, with zero input

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.230
from Perlmutter.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:51.500
Likewise, Perlmutter maintained control of
the comic book and TV businesses, without

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.620
input from Feige.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:56.960
One event that drove the split was apparently
the steadfast refusal from Perlmutter and

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.180
his team to allow Feige to pursue films with
female and non-white leads.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.600
After Feige gained full control, one of the
first things he did was put Black Panther

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:10.280
and Captain Marvel into production and the
two films both made more than $1 billion at

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:15.360
the box office and now rank as the two highest-grossing
solo franchise-starters in the MCU.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:20.500
The TV side of the business, however, has
not had the same kind of success as the MCU.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:25.340
While Marvel's MCU movies are now the highest-grossing
franchise of all time, Marvel TV has failed

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.600
to make much of an impact.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.670
With Feige running the show, and with series
like Ghost Rider no longer in the hopper,

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.140
what will the future of Marvel TV look like?

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.500
Odds are, it's going to look an awful lot
like the MCU.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:40.960
Even before Feige inherited the TV side of
things, he was already spearheading Marvel

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.860
Studios' invasion of the medium via a number
of upcoming Disney+ series with more direct

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:46.980
MCU connections.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.000
But other networks also have Marvel TV series
namely ABC, Freeform, and Hulu.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.280
So what will become of them?

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.180
Well, Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. is ending on
ABC of its own accord in 2020.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:02.060
Hulu's The Runaways was renewed for a third
season prior to the Marvel TV shakeup, while

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:05.420
a third season for Freeform's Cloak &amp; Dagger
has yet to be announced.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.690
There's also a slew of leftover Loeb projects
in development at Hulu, including five animated

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:15.020
series and the live-action Helstrom, but it's
unclear if Feige will keep them around.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:19.680
One defect that has plagued all of Marvel's
previous TV efforts was the tenuous connection

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:20.720
to the MCU.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:24.920
Though most of the series were meant to exist
in the same universe as Feige's films, they

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:25.840
never felt like it.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:30.120
But with Feige now running Marvel TV, too,
you can bet that will change.

